cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SoundFieldUQ: certified sound-field reconstruction with exactly known covariate-shift weights"
message: "If you use this code, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chakraborty
    given-names: Ashmita
version: 0.2.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YOUR-GITHUB-USERNAME/SoundFieldUQ"
abstract: >-
  Distribution-free uncertainty quantification for sparse sound-field
  reconstruction. Because the calibration microphone positions and the listener
  positions to be certified are both designed by the experimenter, the
  covariate-shift likelihood ratio is exactly computable from geometry rather
  than estimated. Weighted conformal prediction with that exact ratio restores
  marginal validity where split conformal fails silently, abstains where no
  measurement constrains the query point, and yields a distribution-free
  microphone-placement criterion. Base MATLAB, no toolboxes, no hardware.
keywords:
  - sound field reconstruction
  - conformal prediction
  - covariate shift
  - uncertainty quantification
  - microphone placement
  - room acoustics
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Conformal Prediction Under Covariate Shift"
    authors:
      - family-names: Tibshirani
        given-names: "Ryan J."
      - family-names: Barber
        given-names: "Rina Foygel"
      - family-names: Candès
        given-names: "Emmanuel J."
      - family-names: Ramdas
        given-names: Aaditya
    year: 2019
    notes: "arXiv:1904.06019 — the construction this project supplies exact weights for"
